PowerShell cmdlets that write, by full name (in either dialect) or alias (PowerShell only): the Set-Content/
Add-Content/Out-File/Tee-Object/Set-Item/New-Item family write their paths;
Remove-Item deletes them as trees; Copy-Item writes the destination and DEST\<name> (a tree with
-Recurse); Move-Item and Rename-Item move whole directories, so source and target are trees;
Invoke-WebRequest/Invoke-RestMethod write their -OutFile; Expand-Archive rewrites its destination
tree. A path may be an array (a,b), each element checked too, and carry a provider prefix (FileSystem::C:\x).

 without , for the engine's own escape sequences only (Levi's colours);
text from the project never goes here unless  has made it printable. Null means
 is not wrapped.

lockflight review status [--feature id] — read only: the feature's review runs, its open, fixed and dismissed findings,
and the summary for the pull request body, which also names the tests a person amended after their red. The agent runs it;
only this, not the agent's own reading, says a finding is closed.

